<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dominique Mbonyumutwa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dominique Mbonyumutwa was a Rwandan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> politician and sub-chief. On 1 November 1959 he was attacked by young Tutsi activists, and false rumours of his death set off the violence against Tutsi chiefs that began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rwandan-revolution">Rwandan Revolution</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhanga">Gitarama</a> declaration of January 1961 he became the provisional first president of the Republic of Rwanda, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregoire-kayibanda">Grégoire Kayibanda</a>.</p></div>
